-- A function whose bindings spilled past the emitter's local limit (O11):
-- 300 where bindings in ONE function leave 180 plain locals plus the `_v`
-- spill table, and a lambda over all of them captured the 180 plus `_v`.
-- The function has no room for a routing table under the emitter's own
-- limit, but the pass runs last and may spend the margin up to the host's
-- 200 active locals, so the captures are routed. Shapes: a lambda applied
-- at once, a lambda under map, and a thunk, each over the 300 bindings.

